# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the two households the rule presses
# Hesh hands in the barns at Haldane's for the harvest. The rule (the board's residency minute, e1.board) is the
# pressure; Josh Brack and George Orme decide, in written scenes.
@household e1_sallis
name: The Sallises, in the barns
street: haldane_yard
people: hesh
hesh: 1
place: q_yard
members: Arn, Ketti, Davin
taken: 0
portion: 1

@household e1_tesk
name: The Tesks, on the hill
street: haldane_yard
people: hesh
hesh: 1
place: q_hill
members: Tesk, Kel
taken: 0
portion: 1

@fate f.e1_sallis
pressure: has(e1.rule_passed)
subject: household e1_sallis
decider: JOSH
scene: e1.frost.decide, e1.frost.sent, e1.frost.kept
window: 7
who: Ketti
because: the board's minute says seasonal hands are not residents; Josh Brack reads the frost list at the post and says who goes up the hill road and who is written down as kept

@fate f.e1_kel
pressure: has(e1.rule_passed)
subject: household e1_tesk
decider: GEORGE
scene: e1.kel.decide, e1.kel.kept, e1.kel.walked
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Kel
because: under the minute any charge is a reason to send a hand up the hill; George Orme says whether the boy is docked and kept or walked to the post with the sweepings in his boots
